Subject: [PATCH] Stop the collision block scan from asking air for a box

World.getCubes is what Entity.move spends its time in - 14.23% of the server thread in a
profile at 0218, 11.69% of it under move alone, which runs the scan twice for a mob that
can step up. Three things in it were work the answer never depended on.

Air reached Block.addCollisionBoxes and then Block.getCollisionBounds, two virtual calls,
to be told what BlockAir answers unconditionally: no box. Those two frames were 4.09% of
the thread, and the box an entity moves through is mostly air. Testing the block reference
first also means the scratch position is only written for blocks that can contribute one -
inside the border it is not needed before that point at all.

The world border's four edges are fixed for the whole call but were read from the border
object once per chunk visited; WorldBorder.maxZ alone was 1.02% of the thread. They are
also only needed when the entity is inside the border.

The PaperSpigot rule letting falling blocks and TNT collide with signs depends on the
config and the entity, and was two instanceof tests and a config read per block.

Verified against the previous jar with the ghost harness, three runs each: live entity
counts, spawn and destroy totals and position corrections are indistinguishable, so the
4,000 golems are still standing on the terrain rather than falling through it.

Measured +1.45% TPS, 6/6 pairwise wins, at 30,000 golems with four bots.

